    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "m8wjom",
      "x": 3280,
      "y": 23538,
      "name": "Note — Helm admin mapping banner is conditional",
      "width": 640,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "Conditional — “Helm-configured admin mapping” banner (HelmAdminMappingWarning / PI0aX)\n\nRenders only when the Helm-seeded admin mapping is non-empty, i.e. installTimeSettings.oidcHelmProvider.roleMappings.admin has at least one group. The mock shows it unconditionally; in the build it is hidden when that list is empty or absent.\n\nIt is an advisory, not a gate: Helm-seeded admin mappings arrive without the FR-015 confirm dialog, so the banner is the only warning the admin sees for them."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "I96cW",
      "x": -16887,
      "y": 24145,
      "name": "Note — Confirm Admin Mapping trigger rule",
      "width": 560,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "Trigger rule — Gameplane/Dialog/Confirm Admin Mapping\n\nFires on chip-add, not on Save: in RoleMappingOverridesCard, handleAddGroup (web/src/routes/AdminSettings.tsx, ~L1535-1544) sets confirmingRole to \"admin\" unconditionally whenever role === \"admin\" and no confirmation is already in progress (`if (role === \"admin\" && !confirmingRole)`) — it does not check whether the admin role's existing effective group list is non-empty or whether the added group changes it. <ConfirmDialog open={confirmingRole === \"admin\"}> (~L1734) renders from that state — well before the section's Save/PUT. It gates the individual group addition to the admin role, not the request: the admin confirms per group-add, and the resulting group list is only included in the PUT once the section is later saved.\n\nIt fires on exactly ONE surface: RoleMappingOverridesCard, the Helm-seeded provider's override editor (auth.helmOverride.roleMappings.admin). The Helm-seeded provider's read-only summary (HelmOIDCProviderCard, ~L1415-1472) displays installTimeSettings.oidcHelmProvider.roleMappings with no mutating path; AuthSection's provider list (providers[]) has no roleMappings editor anywhere — it only toggles enabled and deletes rows. AddProviderForm (~L425-656) has no ConfirmDialog either — new providers cannot set an admin mapping through a confirm step today.\n\nIt is unconditional on group size — Gameplane cannot enumerate IdP group membership, so a one-person group and a 500-person org unit are indistinguishable at confirm time. There is no \"large group\" threshold to check against.\n\nClient-side guard only (FR-015). The API does not enforce or record the confirmation; it accepts the PUT if validation passes."
    },
