    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "R6iab",
      "x": 17780,
      "y": 23635,
      "name": "Note — Role mapping overrides error states",
      "width": 700,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "Error states — Role mapping overrides (PUT /admin/config/auth)\n\nThis screen is the rejected-save variant of “Screen/Admin Settings — Authentication”. Both treatments are conditional and absent on the happy path.\n\nField level — a blank group name is rejected client-side before the PUT: the input takes a destructive border and “Group name can't be blank.” appears under the row. Add stays disabled while the field is empty.\n\nCard level — Gameplane/Error Banner at the foot of the card content, above the actions. One message per response:\n• 400 — “Save failed (400): validation failed — <details from the API>. No changes were saved.”\n• 401 — session expired; redirect to login rather than showing the banner.\n• 403 — “You don't have permission to change role mappings (config:manage required).”\n• 500 — “Save failed (500): the server couldn't store the change. Nothing was saved — try again.”\n\nThe banner clears on the next successful save. The editor keeps the admin's unsaved edits on screen so nothing is lost to a failed request."
    },
