    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "x71Cb",
      "x": 19280,
      "y": 24463,
      "name": "Note — FR-015 confirm step on this surface",
      "width": 640,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "Confirm step — designed intent, NOT YET IMPLEMENTED on this surface\n\nThe design specifies that clicking “Add provider” on this form should reuse Gameplane/Dialog/Confirm Admin Mapping (Kp48V) unmodified, the same way RoleMappingOverridesCard's chip-add flow already does (see I96cW): its text (“Mapping users to the admin role grants full cluster control… Anyone in these groups gets full admin access from their next login.”) already reads correctly for a freshly-typed admin group, not just for the Role Mapping Overrides Card it was first built for. Chips shown in the dialog would list whatever was typed into Admin groups above (e.g. “ops-leads”).\n\nSTATUS: outstanding. AddProviderForm.submit() (web/src/routes/AdminSettings.tsx, ~L478-513) currently calls AuthProviders.putSecret() then onAdd() and closes the form directly — there is no ConfirmDialog invocation anywhere in that component. The confirm step described above and by the AdminGroupsInlineWarning banner is intended behavior this design specifies; the code change to wire Kp48V into AddProviderForm.submit() is still owed.\n\nThe inline AdminGroupsInlineWarning banner added to the Admin groups field on this screen is new, and describes THIS surface (the new-provider form), not the Helm override editor. It differs from the Helm card's HelmAdminMappingWarning (PI0aX) on purpose: that one exists BECAUSE there is no confirm step planned for Helm-seeded mappings; this banner exists on a surface where a confirm step is designed but not yet built. The banner copy (u0KXn) deliberately reads as the designed end state — including “You'll be asked to confirm before this is saved.” — describing what this surface is specified to do once AddProviderForm.submit() is wired to Kp48V, not what the code does today. Keep that copy as-is: this is a design-first repo, the design leads and the implementation follows. The owed work is the React change above, not a rewrite of the banner."
    },
